  "subsystem": {
    "files": [
      "src/runtime/sparse_array.rs"
    ],
    "id": "runtime/sparse-array",
    "mechanism": "the sixteen-way tree is a raw tree of *mut *mut c_void nodes reached by pointer arithmetic (p.add(i), (*p.add(i)).cast::<..>()), raw dereferences and a transmute trampoline. The reconstruction models it as an owned enum Node whose children are owned OwnedNodes and whose deepest slots are the caller's values, and every descent, growth and walk is safe indexing/recursion on that value. Two hardening fixes make it airtight: (A) every node and the header are allocated through the crate's allocator seam (CRYPTO_zalloc) and released with CRYPTO_free by an OwnedNode that derefs to safe indexing, so a caller's installed allocator observes every allocation and exhaustion returns the 0 ossl_sa_set propagates rather than aborting; and (B) the doall walk snapshots its leaves before calling back, so a callback that re-enters the array to clear the slot it was handed (property/store.rs's alg_cleanup) is sound.",
    "why_internal": "OpenSslSa is pub(crate), #[no_mangle] nowhere, and exports no symbol: no public OpenSSL ABI symbol depends on its internals being raw. Its handle crosses into property/store.rs and rsa/ossl.rs only as an opaque *mut c_void, and no C reads its layout. The three observable fields (levels, top, nelem) and every entry-point signature are unchanged."
  },
